(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA) '
(MINISTRY OF EDUCATION) '
(DEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY / HIGHER EDUCATION) '
T*
(NATIONAL EDUCATION POLICY 2020 [NEP 2020]) '
T*
(1. POLICY VISION AND GOALS) '
(The National Education Policy 2020 [NEP 2020], approved by the Union Cabinet on 29th ) '
(July 2020, outlines the vision of India's new education system replacing the previous ) '
(policy of 1986. The policy aims to transform India into a vibrant knowledge society ) '
(and global knowledge superpower by making both school and higher education more ) '
(holistic, flexible, multidisciplinary, suited to 21st-century needs, and aimed at ) '
(bringing out the unique capabilities of each student.) '
T*
(2. KEY STRUCTURAL REFORMS IN SCHOOL EDUCATION) '
(- Transition from 10+2 structure to a new 5+3+3+4 pedagogical structure corresponding ) '
(to ages 3-8 [Foundational], 8-11 [Preparatory], 11-14 [Middle], and 14-18 ) '
([Secondary].) '
(- Foundational Literacy and Numeracy [FLN] identified as an urgent national mission ) '
([NIPUN Bharat].) '
(- Medium of instruction wherever possible until at least Grade 5 [and preferably till ) '
(Grade 8 and beyond] to be mother tongue / local language / regional language.) '
(- Experiential learning, critical thinking, coding from Grade 6, vocational crafts, ) '
(and elimination of rigid separations between arts and sciences.) '
T*
(3. HIGHER EDUCATION REFORMS) '
(- Target Gross Enrolment Ratio [GER] in higher education to reach 50% by 2035.) '
(- Holistic undergraduate education with flexible multi-disciplinary entry and exit ) '
(points [Certificate after 1 yr, Diploma after 2 yrs, Bachelor's after 3 yrs, ) '
(Bachelor's with Research after 4 yrs].) '
(- Academic Bank of Credits [ABC] for digital credit storage and mobility.) '
(- Establishment of Higher Education Commission of India [HECI] as a single ) '
(overarching regulatory umbrella.) '
T*
(4. TARGET YEARS AND INVESTMENT) '
(- Target Year for 100% Gross Enrolment Ratio in preschool to secondary level: 2030.) '
(- Public investment in education to reach 6% of GDP jointly by Central and State ) '
(Governments.) '
T*
(5. OFFICIAL PORTAL AND NODAL MINISTRY) '
(- Nodal Ministry: Ministry of Education, Government of India.) '
(- Official Portal: https://www.education.gov.in) '
ET
